| `Linked` asks whether this run is a module another program linked, rather
| than a program of its own. Run on its own, in either output mode, the
| answer is no — and for `code run` it is always no, because an interpreted
| run is a program.
|
| The yes side needs a `--target shared` build, so it lives in
| `tests/hosted_app.rs`.

emit Linked {} to core get where
assert where ∈ LinkedResult
assert where._class = "LinkedResult"
assert where.value ∈ Boolean
assert not where.value

| The bare form means the same thing.
emit Linked to core get again
assert not again.value

| It is a value like any other, so it can steer a decision.
let door = "net_server"
if where.value { door = "membrane" }
assert door = "net_server"
